# tools/oci/BUCK
#
# Build-host OCI tooling for buck2-native OCI base pull, image assembly, and
# registry push.
#
# oya-oci-assemble: Rust binary that reads a base OCI-layout tarball + one or
# more application layer tar.gz files and emits a complete OCI Image Layout
# directory (OCI spec 1.0) with a recomputed manifest, config, and index.
# Runs on the build host (darwin aarch64 or linux aarch64); exec_dep in the
# oci_image rule (tools/oci/defs.bzl).
#
# oya-oci-push: Rust binary that reads an assembled OCI Image Layout directory,
# uploads referenced blobs through the OCI Distribution API, and publishes the
# manifest tag without docker/crane/skopeo. Runs in Buck2/Prow lanes.
#
# oya-oci-pull-base: Rust binary that fetches a pinned single-arch base image
# manifest plus config/layer blobs through the OCI Distribution API and writes
# the OCI Image Layout tree consumed by oya-oci-assemble.
#
# ADDITIVE: the gateway Dockerfile/BuildKit path is untouched.

rust_binary(
    name = "oya-oci-assemble",
    srcs = glob(["crates/oya-oci-assemble/src/**/*.rs"]),
    crate_root = "crates/oya-oci-assemble/src/main.rs",
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
    deps = [
